{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790260904,"nonce":"DIdbmeu5zaJnXEQFZUVpvMkUg6Y=","title":"Lua: a class field stored where the types do not see it reads back as a reinterpreted box","message":"A slot typed from the constructors (Int or nil, or nil) is read through the\nclass chain, and the chain answers with a value the class got through a store\nthe typer never sees: a mixin helper storing under computed keys, an alias\n(`reg[1] = C; reg[1].f = \"s\"`), a load'ed chunk with the class in its\nenvironment, a coroutine body. The read coerces the string to the slot's type\nand prints a large integer. Same output on main dea6d08b and with the l2\nfield-read work, in every tier; lua5.4 prints the string.\n\n    local C = {}\n    C.__index = C\n    local function new(v) return setmetatable({f = v}, C) end\n    local o = new(nil); new(2)\n    local reg = {}\n    reg[1] = C\n    reg[1].f = \"via alias\"\n    print(o.f)          -- lua5.4: via alias\n\n    local function mixin(dst, src) for k, v in pairs(src) do dst[k] = v end end\n    mixin(C, {f = \"mixed\"})\n    print(o.f)          -- lua5.4: mixed\n\nRelated to a8fd3a3 (the other half of the same field type) and to the\nescape holes the l3 package covers.","files":null}]}